4. Synthetic Polling Is Not Real Polling

This distinction must remain part of the system’s permanent architecture.

If 63% of synthetic respondents predictably favor an option, GPT Polls must say:

63% modeled support

not:

63% of people said yes.

No humans necessarily answered the question.

This protects epistemic integrity and prevents simulated consensus from masquerading as observed consensus.

The permanent invariant is:

\boxed{Synthetic\ estimate \neq observed\ human\ response}

GPT Polls can coexist with real polling.

In fact, real-world polling and behavioral data are vital for calibrating the synthetic system.

