8. Privacy Architecture

Privacy cannot be a cosmetic layer added after the system works.

It must be part of the computational design.

Possible protections include:

* explicit consent,
* purpose limitation,
* coarse feature bins,
* aggregation thresholds,
* suppression of rare combinations,
* differential privacy where appropriate,
* removal of direct identifiers,
* deletion controls,
* population-level querying rather than respondent retrieval,
* prohibition on reconstruction attempts,
* restricted sensitive-attribute use,
* provenance attached to every feature,
* expiration or decay of stale information.

A query should generally be permitted to ask:

“How might parents in their thirties respond?”

but not:

“Tell me exactly what respondent #184729 believes and reconstruct who they are.”

The useful object is the field, not the exposed individual.

⸻

9. The Anchor Spine

A recursively learning system risks becoming increasingly self-referential.

GPT Polls therefore requires a set of invariants that adapt much more slowly than the population model.

This is the Anchor Spine.

9.1 Spine

Nearly immutable:

* synthetic response must remain distinguishable from observed response,
* provenance must be retained,
* historical predictions cannot be retroactively rewritten,
* privacy requirements cannot disappear because changing them improves accuracy,
* uncertainty must be represented,
* calibration failures must remain visible,
* sponsored influence cannot silently alter population estimates.

9.2 Bones

Slow-changing:

* population ontology,
* cohort structure,
* major calibration framework,
* sampling methodology.

9.3 Muscle

Regularly adaptive:

* cohort weights,
* correlations,
* preference parameters,
* behavior coefficients,
* contextual interactions.

9.4 Reflexes

Rapidly adaptive:

* slang,
* fashion,
* memes,
* short-lived events,
* temporary sentiment,
* emerging products.

This creates different adaptation half-lives.

The principle is:

\boxed{
Adapt\ the\ map\ aggressively;
preserve\ the\ coordinate\ system\ cautiously.
}

