11. Calibration Ledger

Every testable prediction should be freezeable.

Example:

Model version: OFE-184
Question:
Would you subscribe at $20/month?
Prediction:
Yes: 41%
Observed conversion:
19%
Delta:
-22 percentage points
Possible error sources:
stated/action gap       -9
population weighting    -5
friction underestimated -3
unknown                 -5
Calibration changes:
purchase-intent coefficient adjusted
uncertainty widened
Anchor changes:
NONE

Over thousands of observations, GPT Polls can learn mappings such as:

Synthetic\ stated\ preference
\rightarrow
Human\ stated\ preference
\rightarrow
Human\ realized\ behavior

This may become more useful than raw synthetic prediction itself.

