42. The Dance Metaphor

A useful metaphor is:

Get the population moving, then watch how its movement changes when the tune changes.

Formally:

stimulus
    ↓
population response
    ↓
perturb stimulus
    ↓
observe delta
    ↓
infer sensitivity
    ↓
repeat

The scientific value comes from the controlled perturbation.

Changing the tune is not inherently about controlling people.

It is about discovering:

Which elements of the environment actually matter to them?

This distinction is important.

The system should prefer transparent experimentation and population understanding over covert manipulation.

