63. Core Invariants

The first implementation should preserve at least the following:

Invariant 1

Synthetic responses are never labeled as real respondents.

Invariant 2

Population provenance remains visible.

Invariant 3

Uncertainty cannot be silently discarded.

Invariant 4

Historical predictions cannot be rewritten after outcomes are known.

Invariant 5

Privacy protections remain structurally upstream of inference.

Invariant 6

Measurement and intervention remain distinguishable.

Invariant 7

The system measures its own calibration.

Invariant 8

Model adaptation occurs at multiple time scales.

Invariant 9

Persistent external error outranks internal coherence.

Invariant 10

An aggregate must remain traceable to its population, model, context, and time.

