64. Compact Formal Model

Let synthetic respondent r_i contain latent state:

z_i

Question:

q

Context:

c

Time:

t

Response:

a_i \sim P(a|z_i,q,c,t,M)

Population distribution:

P(A)
=
\sum_i w_i P(a_i)

Perturb context:

c' = c + \delta

Then measure:

\Delta P(A)
=
P(A|c')-P(A|c)

Observed human result:

P_{real}(A)

Calibration error:

E =
P_{real}(A)-P_{synthetic}(A)

Update the adaptive model:

M_{t+1}
=
Update(M_t,E)

subject to Anchor Spine constraints:

M_{t+1}\in\mathcal C

The entire system can therefore be summarized as:

\boxed{
Observe
\rightarrow
Model
\rightarrow
Poll
\rightarrow
Perturb
\rightarrow
Measure\ Delta
\rightarrow
